+# External Audit Brief — Aegis AI Safety Artifacts
+
+Purpose: Provide auditors with an indexed list of artifacts and commands needed to verify detector provenance, SBOMs, signatures, thresholds, evidence bundles and Rekor entries.
+
+Artifacts you will provide (examples and retrieval commands)
+
+1) Detector image(s)
+ - Registry image: <registry>/<repo>/aegis-detectors:<tag>
+ - Verify image signature with cosign:
+   cosign verify --key <COSIGN_KMS_URI> <registry>/<repo>/aegis-detectors:<tag>
+ - Pull SBOM (if generated):
+   syft <registry>/<repo>/aegis-detectors:<tag> -o json > detectors-sbom.json
+
+2) Pinned model artifacts (artifact store)
+ - Example layout: ${ARTIFACT_BASE}/nudenet/classifier-0.2.4.pkl
+ - Verify checksum:
+   aws s3 cp ${ARTIFACT_BASE}/nudenet/checksum.sha256 .
+   aws s3 cp ${ARTIFACT_BASE}/nudenet/classifier-0.2.4.pkl .
+   sha256sum -c checksum.sha256
+ - Verify cosign blob signature (if provided):
+   cosign verify-blob --signature classifier-0.2.4.pkl.sig classifier-0.2.4.pkl
+
+3) thresholds.json (detector calibration)
+ - Location: ${ARTIFACT_BASE}/thresholds/thresholds-<timestamp>.json
+ - Example fetch:
+   aws s3 cp ${ARTIFACT_BASE}/thresholds/thresholds-2026...json .
+ - Show thresholds and the labeled CSV used to compute them (ops/fl/calibration/labeled.csv)
+
+4) DP accounting & policies
+ - DP service endpoint: http://dp-service:8084
+ - Example: check client epsilon:
+   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $DP_AUTH_TOKEN" http://dp-service:8084/eps/<client>
+ - Verify DB snapshot/backup available (RDS / managed db)
+
+5) Evidence bundles & artifacts
+ - Evidence S3 prefix: s3://<audit-bucket>/content_incident/
+ - Example: list recent bundles:
+   aws s3 ls s3://<audit-bucket>/content_incident/
+ - Download a bundle and verify cosign signature (if signed):
+   aws s3 cp s3://<audit-bucket>/content_incident/<bundle>.tar.gz .
+   cosign verify --key <COSIGN_KMS_URI> <bundle>.tar.gz
+ - Rekor entries: using rekor-cli:
+   rekor-cli search --artifact <bundle>.tar.gz --api-url <REKOR_URL>
+
+6) Action logs & approver audit
+ - Review queue logs (Redis dump or exported JSON): explain where review items and approvals are stored.
+ - Approver audit log (approver signing service): /var/log/aegis/approver_audit.log (or S3 export)
+ - Verify approval signatures via cosign verify-blob (approve.sig)
+
+7) Red-team results & remediation artifacts
+ - Red-team CI run logs (provide link or raw logs)
+ - Argo remediation workflow run id and outputs (Argo UI or kubectl get wf -n aegis-ml)
+ - Evidence bundle generated by remediation workflow and its Rekor/cosign proofs
+
+Verification checklist for auditor
+ - Validate cosign signatures on images & blobs.
+ - Validate checksums on pinned model artifacts.
+ - Validate thresholds.json ties back to a labeled dataset (inspect ops/fl/calibration/labeled.csv).
+ - Validate DP service snapshots and that DP accounting API is reachable and records charges.
+ - Validate that Argo remediation workflow was executed and evidence bundle uploaded.
+ - Verify approver signatures via cosign verify-blob and that audit log contains approver identity & timestamp.
+
+Contact & support
+ - Infra owner: infra-team@example.com
+ - Security lead: secops@example.com
+ - ML Ops: mlops@example.com
+
